skos:mappingRelation a rdf:Property, rdf:Property, owl:ObjectProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core>, <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core>;
  rdfs:label "is in mapping relation with"@en, "is in mapping relation with"@en;
  rdfs:comment "These concept mapping relations mirror semantic relations, and the data model defined below is similar (with the exception of skos:exactMatch) to the data model defined for semantic relations. A distinct vocabulary is provided for concept mapping relations, to provide a convenient way to differentiate links within a concept scheme from links between concept schemes. However, this pattern of usage is not a formal requirement of the SKOS data model, and relies on informal definitions of best practice."@en,
    "These concept mapping relations mirror semantic relations, and the data model defined below is similar (with the exception of skos:exactMatch) to the data model defined for semantic relations. A distinct vocabulary is provided for concept mapping relations, to provide a convenient way to differentiate links within a concept scheme from links between concept schemes. However, this pattern of usage is not a formal requirement of the SKOS data model, and relies on informal definitions of best practice."@en;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf skos:semanticRelation, skos:semanticRelation;
  skos:definition "Relates two concepts coming, by convention, from different schemes, and that have comparable meanings"@en,
    "Relates two concepts coming, by convention, from different schemes, and that have comparable meanings"@en .

