  dct:description "Sound pressure level ($SPL$) or sound level is a logarithmic measure of the effective sound pressure of a sound relative to a reference value. It is measured in decibels (dB) above a standard reference level."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "Sound pressure level ($SPL$) or sound level is a logarithmic measure of the effective sound pressure of a sound relative to a reference value. It is measured in decibels (dB) above a standard reference level."^^qudt:LatexString;
