  The $\\textit{BTU (TH) Foot per Square Foot Hour Degree Fahrenheit}$ is an Imperial unit for 'Thermal Conductivity' defined as:
  $$Btu_{th} \\cdot ft/(h \\cdot ft^2 \\cdot degF)$$.
