unit:C-M a qudt:Unit, qudt:Unit, qudt:DerivedUnit, qudt:DerivedUnit;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/unit>, <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit>;
  rdfs:label "Coulomb Meter"@en-US, "Coulomb Meter"@en-US, "Coulombmeter"@de, "Coulombmeter"@de,
    "coulomb meter"@ms, "coulomb meter"@ms, "coulomb metr"@cs, "coulomb metr"@cs, "coulomb metre"@en,
    "coulomb metre"@en, "coulomb metre"@tr, "coulomb metre"@tr, "coulomb per metro"@it,
    "coulomb per metro"@it, "coulomb-metro"@pt, "coulomb-metro"@pt, "coulomb-metru"@ro,
    "coulomb-metru"@ro, "coulomb-mètre"@fr, "coulomb-mètre"@fr, "culombio metro"@es, "culombio metro"@es,
    "кулон-метр"@ru, "кулон-метр"@ru, "كولوم متر"@ar, "كولوم متر"@ar, "نیوتون متر"@fa,
    "نیوتون متر"@fa, "कूलम्ब मीटर"@hi, "कूलम्ब मीटर"@hi, "クーロンメートル"@ja, "クーロンメートル"@ja,
    "库伦米"@zh, "库伦米"@zh;
  dct:description """
  The $\\text{Coulomb Meter (C-m)}$ is a unit in the category of Electric dipole moment. 
  It is also known as atomic unit, u.a., au, ua. 
  This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. 
  Coulomb Meter (C-m) has a dimension of LTI where $L$ is length, $T$ is time, and $I$ is electric current. 
  This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.
  """^^qudt:LatexString,
    """
  The $\\text{Coulomb Meter (C-m)}$ is a unit in the category of Electric dipole moment. 
  It is also known as atomic unit, u.a., au, ua. 
  This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. 
  Coulomb Meter (C-m) has a dimension of LTI where $L$ is length, $T$ is time, and $I$ is electric current. 
  This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.
  """^^qudt:LatexString;
