  dct:description "The moment of inertia, also called mass moment of inertia, rotational inertia, polar moment of inertia of mass, or the angular mass is a property of a distribution of mass in space that measures its resistance to rotational acceleration about an axis."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "The moment of inertia, also called mass moment of inertia, rotational inertia, polar moment of inertia of mass, or the angular mass is a property of a distribution of mass in space that measures its resistance to rotational acceleration about an axis."^^qudt:LatexString;
