  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AngularAcceleration", "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AngularAcceleration";
  dct:description "Angular acceleration is the rate of change of angular velocity over time. Measurement of the change made in the rate of change of an angle that a spinning object undergoes per unit time. It is a vector quantity.  Also called Rotational acceleration. In SI units, it is measured in radians per second squared ($rad/s^2$), and is usually denoted by the Greek letter alpha."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "Angular acceleration is the rate of change of angular velocity over time. Measurement of the change made in the rate of change of an angle that a spinning object undergoes per unit time. It is a vector quantity.  Also called Rotational acceleration. In SI units, it is measured in radians per second squared ($rad/s^2$), and is usually denoted by the Greek letter alpha."^^qudt:LatexString;
  skos:broader quantitykind:InverseTime_Squared, quantitykind:InverseTime_Squared;
