  dct:description "The Angular Impulse, also known as angular momentum, is the moment of linear momentum around a point. It is defined as$H = \\int Mdt$, where $M$ is the moment of force and $t$ is time."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "The Angular Impulse, also known as angular momentum, is the moment of linear momentum around a point. It is defined as$H = \\int Mdt$, where $M$ is the moment of force and $t$ is time."^^qudt:LatexString;
  skos:altLabel "Drehmomentstoß"@de, "Drehmomentstoß"@de;
