quantitykind:MassRatio a qudt:QuantityKind, qudt:QuantityKind;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>, <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "Mass Ratio"@en, "Mass Ratio"@en;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:MassRatio", "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:MassRatio";
  dct:description "In aerospace engineering, mass ratio is a measure of the efficiency of a rocket. It describes how much more massive the vehicle is with propellant than without; that is, it is the ratio of the rocket's wet mass (vehicle plus contents plus propellant) to its dry mass (vehicle plus contents)"^^qudt:LatexString,
    "In aerospace engineering, mass ratio is a measure of the efficiency of a rocket. It describes how much more massive the vehicle is with propellant than without; that is, it is the ratio of the rocket's wet mass (vehicle plus contents plus propellant) to its dry mass (vehicle plus contents)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:hasDimensionVector dimensionvector:A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1, dimensionvector:A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1;
  qudt:iec61360Code "0112/2///62720#UAD109", "0112/2///62720#UAD109";
  qudt:informativeReference "https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec61987/iec61987.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD109"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec61987/iec61987.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD109"^^xsd:anyURI;
  qudt:symbol "R or M_{R}", "R or M_{R}";
  qudt:plainTextDescription "In aerospace engineering, mass ratio is a measure of the efficiency of a rocket. It describes how much more massive the vehicle is with propellant than without; that is, it is the ratio of the rocket's wet mass (vehicle plus contents plus propellant) to its dry mass (vehicle plus contents)",
    "In aerospace engineering, mass ratio is a measure of the efficiency of a rocket. It describes how much more massive the vehicle is with propellant than without; that is, it is the ratio of the rocket's wet mass (vehicle plus contents plus propellant) to its dry mass (vehicle plus contents)";
  qudt:applicableUnit unit:FemtoGM-PER-KiloGM, unit:FemtoGM-PER-KiloGM, unit:GM-PER-GM,
