  rdfs:label "Galileo"@en, "Galileo"@en;
  dct:description "The $\\textit{Galileo}$ is the unit of acceleration of free fall used extensively in the science of gravimetry. The Galileo is defined as $1 \\textit{centimeter per square second}$ ($1 cm/s^2$). Unfortunately, the Galileo is often denoted with the symbol Gal, not to be confused with the Gallon that also uses the same symbol."^^qudt:LatexString,
