  qudt:symbol "0173-1#Z4-BAJ448#002", "0173-1#Z4-BAJ448#002";
  qudt:plainTextDescription "A torsional spring constant is a measure of the stiffness of a torsional spring, which is a type of spring that experiences twisting or torque rather than compression or extension. It is typically measured in newton-meters per radian (N·m/rad) and is used to calculate the amount of torque required to twist a spring a certain amount. It is related to the spring's geometry, material properties, and manufacturing process.",
    "A torsional spring constant is a measure of the stiffness of a torsional spring, which is a type of spring that experiences twisting or torque rather than compression or extension. It is typically measured in newton-meters per radian (N·m/rad) and is used to calculate the amount of torque required to twist a spring a certain amount. It is related to the spring's geometry, material properties, and manufacturing process.",
