  dct:description "\"Length Per Unit Magnetic Flux\" is the the resistance of a material to the establishment of a magnetic field in it. It is the reciprocal of $\\textit{Magnetic Permeability}$, the inverse of the measure of the ability of a material to support the formation of a magnetic field within itself."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "\"Length Per Unit Magnetic Flux\" is the the resistance of a material to the establishment of a magnetic field in it. It is the reciprocal of $\\textit{Magnetic Permeability}$, the inverse of the measure of the ability of a material to support the formation of a magnetic field within itself."^^qudt:LatexString;
