  qudt:plainTextDescription "Length Per Unit Magnetic Flux is the the resistance of a material to the establishment of a magnetic field in it. It is the reciprocal of Magnetic Permeability, the inverse of the measure of the ability of a material to support the formation of a magnetic field within itself.",
