  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ForcePerElectricCharge",
    "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ForcePerElectricCharge";
  dct:description "The electric field depicts the force exerted on other electrically charged objects by the electrically charged particle the field is surrounding. The electric field is a vector field with SI units of newtons per coulomb ($N C^{-1}$) or, equivalently, volts per metre ($V m^{-1}$ ). The SI base units of the electric field are $kg m s^{-3} A^{-1}$. The strength or magnitude of the field at a given point is defined as the force that would be exerted on a positive test charge of 1 coulomb placed at that point"^^qudt:LatexString,
    "The electric field depicts the force exerted on other electrically charged objects by the electrically charged particle the field is surrounding. The electric field is a vector field with SI units of newtons per coulomb ($N C^{-1}$) or, equivalently, volts per metre ($V m^{-1}$ ). The SI base units of the electric field are $kg m s^{-3} A^{-1}$. The strength or magnitude of the field at a given point is defined as the force that would be exerted on a positive test charge of 1 coulomb placed at that point"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:hasDimensionVector dimensionvector:A0E-1L1I0M1H0T-3D0, dimensionvector:A0E-1L1I0M1H0T-3D0;
  qudt:informativeReference "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_field"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_field"^^xsd:anyURI;
  qudt:applicableUnit unit:N-PER-C, unit:N-PER-C .

