  qudt:latexDefinition "$\\varphi = p / p_{sat}$, where $p$ is partial pressure of vapour,  $p_{sat}$ is thermodynamic temperature and $V$ is its partial pressure at saturation (at the same temperature). Relative partial pressure is often referred to as $RH$ and expressed in percent. $\\textit{Relative Partial Pressure}$ is also referred to as $\\textit{Relative Humidity}$."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "$\\varphi = p / p_{sat}$, where $p$ is partial pressure of vapour,  $p_{sat}$ is thermodynamic temperature and $V$ is its partial pressure at saturation (at the same temperature). Relative partial pressure is often referred to as $RH$ and expressed in percent. $\\textit{Relative Partial Pressure}$ is also referred to as $\\textit{Relative Humidity}$."^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:applicableUnit unit:PERCENT, unit:PERCENT .

