qudt:QuantityValue a owl:Class, owl:Class;
  rdfs:subClassOf qudt:Concept, qudt:Concept, qudt:Quantifiable, qudt:Quantifiable,
    _:6bb918f5130b4a77805c72ffff92bd8c675, _:6bb918f5130b4a77805c72ffff92bd8c676, _:b1cb43fcbd504833bf8a964862c3127019440;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/schema/qudt>, <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt>;
  rdfs:label "Quantity value", "Quantity value";
  rdfs:comment "A <i>Quantity Value</i> expresses the magnitude and kind of a quantity and is given by the product of a numerical value <code>n</code> and a unit of measure <code>U</code>. The number multiplying the unit is referred to as the numerical value of the quantity expressed in that unit. Refer to <a href=\"http://physics.nist.gov/Pubs/SP811/sec07.html\">NIST SP 811 section 7</a> for more on quantity values."^^rdf:HTML,
    "A <i>Quantity Value</i> expresses the magnitude and kind of a quantity and is given by the product of a numerical value <code>n</code> and a unit of measure <code>U</code>. The number multiplying the unit is referred to as the numerical value of the quantity expressed in that unit. Refer to <a href=\"http://physics.nist.gov/Pubs/SP811/sec07.html\">NIST SP 811 section 7</a> for more on quantity values."^^rdf:HTML .

