qudt:SolidAngleUnit a owl:Class, owl:Class;
  rdfs:subClassOf qudt:AngleUnit, qudt:AngleUnit;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/schema/qudt>, <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt>;
  rdfs:label "Solid Angle Unit", "Solid Angle Unit";
  dct:description "The solid angle subtended by a surface S is defined as the surface area of a unit sphere covered by the surface S's projection onto the sphere. A solid angle is related to the surface of a sphere in the same way an ordinary angle is related to the circumference of a circle. Since the total surface area of the unit sphere is 4*pi, the measure of solid angle will always be between 0 and 4*pi.",
    "The solid angle subtended by a surface S is defined as the surface area of a unit sphere covered by the surface S's projection onto the sphere. A solid angle is related to the surface of a sphere in the same way an ordinary angle is related to the circumference of a circle. Since the total surface area of the unit sphere is 4*pi, the measure of solid angle will always be between 0 and 4*pi." .

