  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ForcePerArea", "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ForcePerArea";
  dct:description """The ambient pressure on an object is the pressure of the surrounding medium, such as a gas or liquid, which comes into contact with the object.
The SI unit of pressure is the pascal (Pa), which is a very small unit relative to atmospheric pressure on Earth, so kilopascals ($kPa$) are more commonly used in this context. """^^qudt:LatexString,
