quantitykind:VoltagePhasor a qudt:QuantityKind, qudt:QuantityKind;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>, <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "Voltage Phasor"@en, "Voltage Phasor"@en;
  dct:description "\"Voltage Phasor\" is a representation of voltage as a sinusoidal integral quantity using a complex quantity whose argument is equal to the initial phase and whose modulus is equal to the root-mean-square value. A phasor is a constant complex number, usually expressed in exponential form, representing the complex amplitude (magnitude and phase) of a sinusoidal function of time. Phasors are used by electrical engineers to simplify computations involving sinusoids, where they can often reduce a differential equation problem to an algebraic one."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "\"Voltage Phasor\" is a representation of voltage as a sinusoidal integral quantity using a complex quantity whose argument is equal to the initial phase and whose modulus is equal to the root-mean-square value. A phasor is a constant complex number, usually expressed in exponential form, representing the complex amplitude (magnitude and phase) of a sinusoidal function of time. Phasors are used by electrical engineers to simplify computations involving sinusoids, where they can often reduce a differential equation problem to an algebraic one."^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:hasDimensionVector dimensionvector:A0E-1L2I0M1H0T-3D0, dimensionvector:A0E-1L2I0M1H0T-3D0;
  qudt:informativeReference "http://www.iso.org/iso/home/store/catalogue_tc/catalogue_detail.htm?csnumber=31891"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "http://www.iso.org/iso/home/store/catalogue_tc/catalogue_detail.htm?csnumber=31891"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-11-26"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-11-26"^^xsd:anyURI;
  qudt:plainTextDescription "\"Voltage Phasor\" is a representation of voltage as a sinusoidal integral quantity using a complex quantity whose argument is equal to the initial phase and whose modulus is equal to the root-mean-square value. A phasor is a constant complex number, usually expressed in exponential form, representing the complex amplitude (magnitude and phase) of a sinusoidal function of time. Phasors are used by electrical engineers to simplify computations involving sinusoids, where they can often reduce a differential equation problem to an algebraic one.",
    "\"Voltage Phasor\" is a representation of voltage as a sinusoidal integral quantity using a complex quantity whose argument is equal to the initial phase and whose modulus is equal to the root-mean-square value. A phasor is a constant complex number, usually expressed in exponential form, representing the complex amplitude (magnitude and phase) of a sinusoidal function of time. Phasors are used by electrical engineers to simplify computations involving sinusoids, where they can often reduce a differential equation problem to an algebraic one.";
  qudt:latexSymbol "$\\underline{U}$"^^qudt:LatexString, "$\\underline{U}$"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:latexDefinition "When $u = \\hat{U} \\cos{(\\omega t + \\alpha)}$, where $u$ is the voltage, $\\omega$ is angular frequency, $t$ is time, and $\\alpha$ is initial phase, then $\\underline{U} = Ue^{ja}$."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "When $u = \\hat{U} \\cos{(\\omega t + \\alpha)}$, where $u$ is the voltage, $\\omega$ is angular frequency, $t$ is time, and $\\alpha$ is initial phase, then $\\underline{U} = Ue^{ja}$."^^qudt:LatexString .

quantitykind:ElectricPower a qudt:QuantityKind, qudt:QuantityKind;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>, <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "Wirkleistung"@de, "Wirkleistung"@de, "electric power"@en, "electric power"@en,
    "moc czynna"@pl, "moc czynna"@pl, "potencia activa"@es, "potencia activa"@es, "potenza attiva"@it,
    "potenza attiva"@it, "potência activa"@pt, "potência activa"@pt, "puissance active"@fr,
    "puissance active"@fr, "القدرة الفعالة"@ar, "القدرة الفعالة"@ar, "有功功率"@zh, "有功功率"@zh,
    "有効電力"@ja, "有効電力"@ja;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Power", "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ElectricPower";
  dct:description "\"Electric Power\" is the rate at which electrical energy is transferred by an electric circuit. In the simple case of direct current circuits, electric power can be calculated as the product of the potential difference in the circuit (V) and the amount of current flowing in the circuit (I): $P = VI$, where $P$ is the power, $V$ is the potential difference, and $I$ is the current. However, in general electric power is calculated by taking the integral of the vector cross-product of the electrical and magnetic fields over a specified area."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "\"Electric Power\" is the rate at which electrical energy is transferred by an electric circuit. In the simple case of direct current circuits, electric power can be calculated as the product of the potential difference in the circuit (V) and the amount of current flowing in the circuit (I): $P = VI$, where $P$ is the power, $V$ is the potential difference, and $I$ is the current. However, in general electric power is calculated by taking the integral of the vector cross-product of the electrical and magnetic fields over a specified area."^^qudt:LatexString;
  skos:broader quantitykind:Power, quantitykind:Power;
  qudt:hasDimensionVector dimensionvector:A0E0L2I0M1H0T-3D0, dimensionvector:A0E0L2I0M1H0T-3D0;
  qudt:symbol "P_E", "P_E";
  qudt:latexDefinition "$p = ui$, where $u$ is instantaneous voltage and $i$ is instantaneous electric current."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "$p = ui$, where $u$ is instantaneous voltage and $i$ is instantaneous electric current."^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:applicableUnit unit:BAR-L-PER-SEC, unit:BAR-M3-PER-SEC, unit:BTU_IT-PER-HR, unit:BTU_IT-PER-SEC,
    unit:ERG-PER-SEC, unit:ExaJ-PER-SEC, unit:ExaW, unit:ExaW, unit:FT-LB_F-PER-HR, unit:FT-LB_F-PER-MIN,
    unit:FT-LB_F-PER-SEC, unit:GigaJ-PER-HR, unit:GigaJ-PER-SEC, unit:GigaW, unit:GigaW,
    unit:HP, unit:HP_Boiler, unit:HP_Brake, unit:HP_Electric, unit:HP_Metric, unit:HectoPA-L-PER-SEC,
    unit:HectoPA-M3-PER-SEC, unit:J-PER-DAY, unit:J-PER-HR, unit:J-PER-MIN, unit:J-PER-SEC,
