quantitykind:ElectromotiveForce a qudt:QuantityKind, qudt:QuantityKind;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>, <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "Daya gerak elektrik"@ms, "Daya gerak elektrik"@ms, "Elektromotor kuvvet"@tr,
    "Elektromotor kuvvet"@tr, "Elektromotorické napětí"@cs, "Elektromotorické napětí"@cs,
    "electromotive force"@en, "electromotive force"@en, "elektromotorische Kraft"@de,
    "elektromotorische Kraft"@de, "elektromotorna sila"@sl, "elektromotorna sila"@sl,
    "force électromotrice"@fr, "force électromotrice"@fr, "forza elettromotrice"@it, "forza elettromotrice"@it,
    "força eletromotriz"@pt, "força eletromotriz"@pt, "forță electromotoare"@ro, "forță electromotoare"@ro,
    "fuerza electromotriz"@es, "fuerza electromotriz"@es, "siła elektromotoryczna"@pl,
    "siła elektromotoryczna"@pl, "электродвижущая сила"@ru, "электродвижущая сила"@ru,
    "قوة محركة كهربائية"@ar, "قوة محركة كهربائية"@ar, "نیروی محرک الکتریکی"@fa, "نیروی محرک الکتریکی"@fa,
    "विद्युतवाहक बल"@hi, "विद्युतवाहक बल"@hi, "起電力"@ja, "起電力"@ja, "電動勢"@zh, "電動勢"@zh;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:EnergyPerElectricCharge",
    "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:EnergyPerElectricCharge";
  dct:description """
  In physics, $\\textit{Electromotive Force}$, or most commonly $emf$ (seldom capitalized), or (occasionally) electromotance is that which tends to cause current (actual electrons and ions) to flow. 
  More formally, $emf$ is the external work expended per unit of charge to produce an electric potential difference across two open-circuited terminals.
  $\\textit{Electromotive Force}$ is deprecated in the ISO System of Quantities.
  """^^qudt:LatexString,
    """
  In physics, $\\textit{Electromotive Force}$, or most commonly $emf$ (seldom capitalized), or (occasionally) electromotance is that which tends to cause current (actual electrons and ions) to flow. 
  More formally, $emf$ is the external work expended per unit of charge to produce an electric potential difference across two open-circuited terminals.
  $\\textit{Electromotive Force}$ is deprecated in the ISO System of Quantities.
  """^^qudt:LatexString;
  skos:broader quantitykind:EnergyPerElectricCharge, quantitykind:EnergyPerElectricCharge;
  qudt:dbpediaMatch "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Electromotive_force"^^xsd:anyURI, "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Electromotive_force"^^xsd:anyURI;
  qudt:hasDimensionVector dimensionvector:A0E-1L2I0M1H0T-3D0, dimensionvector:A0E-1L2I0M1H0T-3D0;
  qudt:symbol "E", "E";
  qudt:applicableUnit unit:FemtoV, unit:FemtoV, unit:GigaV, unit:GigaV, unit:KiloV,
    unit:KiloV, unit:MegaV, unit:MegaV, unit:MicroV, unit:MicroV, unit:MilliV, unit:MilliV,
    unit:NanoV, unit:NanoV, unit:PicoV, unit:PicoV, unit:PlanckVolt, unit:PlanckVolt,
    unit:TeraV, unit:TeraV, unit:V, unit:V, unit:V_Ab, unit:V_Ab, unit:V_Stat, unit:V_Stat,
    unit:ExaV, unit:PetaV .

quantitykind:ElectronAffinity a qudt:QuantityKind, qudt:QuantityKind;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>, <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "Electron Affinity"@en, "Electron Affinity"@en;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy", "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy";
  dct:description """
  $\\textit{Electron Affinity}$ is the energy difference between an electron at rest at infinity and an electron at the lowest level of the conduction band in an insulator or semiconductor. 
  The amount of energy released when an electron is added to a neutral atom or molecule to form a negative ion.
  """^^qudt:LatexString,
    """
  $\\textit{Electron Affinity}$ is the energy difference between an electron at rest at infinity and an electron at the lowest level of the conduction band in an insulator or semiconductor. 
  The amount of energy released when an electron is added to a neutral atom or molecule to form a negative ion.
  """^^qudt:LatexString;
  skos:broader quantitykind:Energy, quantitykind:Energy;
  qudt:hasDimensionVector dimensionvector:A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0, dimensionvector:A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0;
  qudt:informativeReference "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electron_affinity"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electron_affinity"^^xsd:anyURI;
  qudt:symbol "χ", "χ";
  qudt:plainTextDescription "\"Electron Affinity\" is the energy difference between an electron at rest at infinity and an electron at the lowest level of the conduction band in an insulator or semiconductor. The the amount of energy released when an electron is added to a neutral atom or molecule to form a negative ion.",
    "\"Electron Affinity\" is the energy difference between an electron at rest at infinity and an electron at the lowest level of the conduction band in an insulator or semiconductor. The the amount of energy released when an electron is added to a neutral atom or molecule to form a negative ion.";
