  rdfs:label "Energía de Gibbs"@es, "Energía de Gibbs"@es, "Entalpie liberă"@ro, "Entalpie liberă"@ro,
    "Gibbs Serbest Enerjisi"@tr, "Gibbs Serbest Enerjisi"@tr, "Gibbs energy"@en, "Gibbs energy"@en,
    "Gibbsova volná energie"@cs, "Gibbsova volná energie"@cs, "Prosta entalpija"@sl, "Prosta entalpija"@sl,
    "Tenaga Gibbs"@ms, "Tenaga Gibbs"@ms, "energia libera di Gibbs"@it, "energia libera di Gibbs"@it,
    "energia livre de Gibbs"@pt, "energia livre de Gibbs"@pt, "entalpia swobodna"@pl,
    "entalpia swobodna"@pl, "enthalpie libre"@fr, "enthalpie libre"@fr, "freie Enthalpie"@de,
    "freie Enthalpie"@de, "энергия Гиббса"@ru, "энергия Гиббса"@ru, "انرژی آزاد گیبس"@fa,
    "انرژی آزاد گیبس"@fa, "طاقة غيبس الحرة"@ar, "طاقة غيبس الحرة"@ar, "ギブズエネルギー"@ja, "ギブズエネルギー"@ja,
    "吉布斯自由能"@zh, "吉布斯自由能"@zh;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy", "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy";
  dct:description """
  $\\textit{Internal Energy}$ is one of the potentials are used to measure energy changes in systems as they evolve from an initial state to a final state. 
  The potential used depends on the constraints of the system, such as constant temperature or pressure. 
  $\\textit{Internal Energy}$ is the internal energy of the system, $\\textit{Enthalpy}$ is the internal energy of the system plus the energy related to pressure-volume work,
   and Helmholtz and Gibbs free energy are the energies available in a system to do useful work when the temperature and volume or the pressure and temperature are fixed, respectively. 
  The name $\\textit{Gibbs Free Energy}$ is also used.
  """^^qudt:LatexString,
    """
  $\\textit{Internal Energy}$ is one of the potentials are used to measure energy changes in systems as they evolve from an initial state to a final state. 
  The potential used depends on the constraints of the system, such as constant temperature or pressure. 
  $\\textit{Internal Energy}$ is the internal energy of the system, $\\textit{Enthalpy}$ is the internal energy of the system plus the energy related to pressure-volume work,
   and Helmholtz and Gibbs free energy are the energies available in a system to do useful work when the temperature and volume or the pressure and temperature are fixed, respectively. 
  The name $\\textit{Gibbs Free Energy}$ is also used.
  """^^qudt:LatexString;
  skos:altLabel "Gibbs function"@en, "Gibbs function"@en, "Gibbs-Energie"@de, "Gibbs-Energie"@de,
