quantitykind:EnergyExpenditure a qudt:QuantityKind, qudt:QuantityKind;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.0.0/vocab/quantitykind>, <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind>;
  rdfs:label "Energy Expenditure"@en, "Energy Expenditure"@en;
  dct:description """Energy expenditure is dependent on a person's sex, metabolic rate, body-mass composition, the thermic effects of food, and activity level.  The approximate energy expenditure of a man lying in bed is $1.0\\,kilo\\,calorie\\,per\\,hour\\,per\\,kilogram$. For slow walking (just over two miles per hour), $3.0\\,kilo\\,calorie\\,per\\,hour\\,per\\,kilogram$. For fast steady running (about 10 miles per hour), $16.3\\,kilo\\,calorie\\,per\\,hour\\,per\\,kilogram$.
Females expend about 10 per cent less energy than males of the same size doing a comparable activity.  For people weighing the same, individuals with a high percentage of body fat usually expend less energy than lean people, because fat is not as metabolically active as muscle."""^^qudt:LatexString,
    """Energy expenditure is dependent on a person's sex, metabolic rate, body-mass composition, the thermic effects of food, and activity level.  The approximate energy expenditure of a man lying in bed is $1.0\\,kilo\\,calorie\\,per\\,hour\\,per\\,kilogram$. For slow walking (just over two miles per hour), $3.0\\,kilo\\,calorie\\,per\\,hour\\,per\\,kilogram$. For fast steady running (about 10 miles per hour), $16.3\\,kilo\\,calorie\\,per\\,hour\\,per\\,kilogram$.
Females expend about 10 per cent less energy than males of the same size doing a comparable activity.  For people weighing the same, individuals with a high percentage of body fat usually expend less energy than lean people, because fat is not as metabolically active as muscle."""^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:hasDimensionVector dimensionvector:A0E0L2I0M1H0T-3D0, dimensionvector:A0E0L2I0M1H0T-3D0;
  qudt:informativeReference "http://www.oxfordreference.com/display/10.1093/acref/9780198631477.001.0001/acref-9780198631477-e-594"^^xsd:anyURI,
    "http://www.oxfordreference.com/display/10.1093/acref/acref-9780198631477-e-594"^^xsd:anyURI .

