    "masse au repos"@fr, "rest mass"@en, "rest mass"@en, "инвариантная масса"@ru, "инвариантная масса"@ru,
    "جرم سکون"@fa, "جرم سکون"@fa, "كتلة ساكنة"@ar, "كتلة ساكنة"@ar, "निश्चर द्रव्यमान"@hi,
    "निश्चर द्रव्यमान"@hi, "不変質量"@ja, "不変質量"@ja, "静止质量"@zh, "静止质量"@zh;
  rdfs:comment "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Mass", "Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Mass";
  dct:description "The $\\textit{Rest Mass}$, the invariant mass, intrinsic mass, proper mass, or (in the case of bound systems or objects observed in their center of momentum frame) simply mass, is a characteristic of the total energy and momentum of an object or a system of objects that is the same in all frames of reference related by Lorentz transformations. The mass of a particle type X (electron, proton or neutron) when that particle is at rest. For an electron: $m_e = 9,109 382 15(45) 10^{-31} kg$, for a proton: $m_p = 1,672 621 637(83) 10^{-27} kg$, for a neutron: $m_n = 1,674 927 211(84) 10^{-27} kg$. Rest mass is often denoted $m_0$."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "The $\\textit{Rest Mass}$, the invariant mass, intrinsic mass, proper mass, or (in the case of bound systems or objects observed in their center of momentum frame) simply mass, is a characteristic of the total energy and momentum of an object or a system of objects that is the same in all frames of reference related by Lorentz transformations. The mass of a particle type X (electron, proton or neutron) when that particle is at rest. For an electron: $m_e = 9,109 382 15(45) 10^{-31} kg$, for a proton: $m_p = 1,672 621 637(83) 10^{-27} kg$, for a neutron: $m_n = 1,674 927 211(84) 10^{-27} kg$. Rest mass is often denoted $m_0$."^^qudt:LatexString;
  skos:altLabel "Proper Mass", "Proper Mass", "invariantna masa"@sl, "invariantna masa"@sl,
    "lastna masa"@sl, "lastna masa"@sl, "masa niezmiennicza"@pl, "masa niezmiennicza"@pl,
